{{Quote|Welcome to the Spire on Stygeon Prime, the only Imperial detainment facility in the Stygeon system&mdash;and it's impregnable.|Sabine Wren|<ref name="Old Masters">{{Rebels|Rise of the Old Masters}}</ref>}}
The '''Spire''', also known as the '''Stygeon Prison''', was a secret, remote [[prison]] [[fortress]] built into the [[mountain]]s of the [[planet]] [[Stygeon Prime]]. Its builder and early history were shrouded in mystery and was constructed with similarily thick [[transparisteel]]. It was secretly used during the [[Clone Wars]] by the [[Confederacy of Independent Systems]] before being used by the [[Galactic Empire]] and its [[Inquisitorius]] during the [[Imperial Era]].

During the Clone Wars, the prison was secretly operated by the Confederacy and was where [[Sith Lord]]s [[Darth Sidious]] and [[Darth]] [[Dooku|Tyranus]] held the renegade Sith Lord [[Maul]] in the prison before he [[Escape from the Spire|escaped]] with the help of [[Death Watch]].

[[Standard year|Years]] later, the prison was run by the [[Galactic Empire]] and protected the prison with [[ray shield]]s, blast-proof structures, anti-aircraft weapons, [[TIE/ln space superiority starfighter|TIE fighters]], and [[stormtrooper]]s. The rebellious [[Spectres|crew]] of the ''[[Ghost]]'' learned that the [[Inquisitor]]s was holding [[Jedi Master]] [[Luminara Unduli]] and [[Duel on Stygeon Prime|attempted]] to save her. During the attempt, former [[Padawan]] [[Kanan Jarrus]] encountered [[the Grand Inquisitor]].

==Description==
[[File:Spire_Stygeon.jpg|thumb|right|300px|The Spire sat among the mountains of the planet Stygeon Prime]]
Located on the [[planet]] [[Stygeon Prime]], the Spire was a top-secret fortress built into the [[mountain]]s of one of the planet's most inhospitable areas, its name befitting the structure's architectural formation. Although its builder and early history were shrouded in mystery, the facility was used extensively by the [[Dark Lord of the Sith]] [[Darth Sidious]] before the [[Proclamation of the New Order|rise]] of the [[Galactic Empire]], where it primarily served as a [[Prison|containment facility]].<ref name="BMF 73">{{BuildFalconCite|73|Guide to the Galaxy}}</ref>

Accessible only from the air, entry was gained by one of two docking ports. A small number of windows were built into the Spire's heavy walls, and were constructed with similarily thick [[transparisteel]]. The density of the material distorted the view of anyone hoping to peer out from within, and in turn only allowed thin, weak streaks of light to shine into the facility's interior. Its dingy, claustrophobic atmosphere compounded the already dungeon-like design of the Spire.<ref name="BMF 73" />

Both blast-proof and [[Ray shield|ray-shielded]], the Spire made scanning of any kind impossible. The facility was further protected by ground-to-air weapon systems, each tied in to a sophisticated [[sensor array]], as well as [[Starship|ships]] that patrolled the surrounding area. During the [[Clone Wars]], the facility's [[Standard day|day]]-to-day operations were handled by the [[Confederacy of Independent Systems]] and later the Galactic Empire, whose [[garrison]]s of [[battle droid]]s and [[stormtrooper]]s patrolled the prison's labyrinth of passageways, corridors, tunnels and exterior balconies around the clock.<ref name="BMF 73" />

==History==
[[File:Maul_Guest_of_the_Spire.png|thumb|left|220px|Darth Sidious questions Darth Maul at the Spire]]
During the Clone Wars, the Confederacy of Independent Systems secretly operated the Spire.<ref name="Son of Dathomir 1" /> Following [[Darth]] Sidious' [[Mandalorian Civil War (19 BBY)|capture]] of [[Maul|Darth Maul]] on [[Mandalore]],<ref name="The Lawless">{{TCW|The Lawless}}</ref> Maul was taken by Sidious and his [[Sith apprentice|apprentice]] [[Count]] [[Dooku]] to the Separatist's secret prison on Stygeon Prime. There, Maul was brutally interrogated by Sidious and Dooku. After Sidious left, Dooku continued interrogating Maul for information on his [[Shadow Collective]] and his underworld contacts. However, a pair of [[Mandalorian super commando]]s, [[Commander]] [[Gar Saxon|Saxon]] and [[Rook Kast]], were sent by Mandalore's [[Prime Minister]] [[Almec]] to free Maul. They were able to [[Escape from the Spire|liberate]] Maul, escape the prison and evade the prison's battle droid garrison.<ref name="Son of Dathomir 1" />

[[File:Encounter_at_Stygeon_Prime_TCG-GA.png|thumb|right|250px|The Spire during the Galactic Empire]]
Following the end of the Clone Wars, the Spire came under the control of the newly formed Galactic Empire. After her capture, [[Jedi]] [[Jedi Master|Master]] [[Luminara Unduli]] was imprisoned there and later executed. Her remains were kept in her former cell in order to lure out any survivors of [[Order 66]]. Five [[Standard year|years]] before the [[Battle of Yavin]], Imperial [[senator]] [[Gall Trayvis]], posing as a dissident, leaked information on the Spire, claiming that Master Unduli was alive. The news was received by the [[Spectres|Lothal rebel cell]], who acted on the information, hoping to free her. Cell leader and Jedi [[Kanan Jarrus]] and his team were able to infiltrate the Spire, however Jarrus and his [[Padawan|apprentice]], [[Ezra Bridger]], discovered that Unduli was in fact dead. [[The Grand Inquisitor]] revealed that Unduli had died with the [[Galactic Republic|Republic]] and that her [[bone]]s were meant to lure the last of the Jedi out of hiding. Jarrus [[Duel on Stygeon Prime|dueled]] the Inquisitor, but was outmatched. He and the other rebels were able to make their escape past the Spire's stormtrooper garrison and escape.<ref name="Old Masters" />

